    "summary": "A number of stocks fell in the morning session after concerns grew over a rising number of uninsured patients. The trend was highlighted in HCA Healthcare's recent earnings report, which pointed to a 'negative payer mix shift.' This term refers to a change in the types of insurance patients have, in this case, an increase in uninsured individuals resulting from losses in health insurance exchange coverage. For HCA, this shift was significant, reducing pre-tax income by an estimated $400 million",
